+// ── [Empower] / [Empowered] / Disempower (VEN) ───────────────────────────
+//
+// Three printed things, one latch (GameObject::is_empowered):
+//
+//   [Empower] <cost>       an activated ability: pay it, become Empowered.
+//                          "Use only if not Empowered."
+//   [Empowered][>] <text>  an ability that only works while the latch is set,
+//                          or a clause that reads differently while it is.
+//   Disempower this, <cost>: <effect>
+//                          an activated ability whose cost includes clearing
+//                          the latch — so it is legal only while set.
+//
+// The legality halves are why Card::canActivateAbility grew a per-object,
+// per-ability overload: "use only if not Empowered" is about THIS copy of the
+// card and THIS one of its abilities, and the card-wide form could express
+// neither. Cards using these helpers override that overload and answer from
+// empowerGate().
